news:1107360258.547617.9320@z14g2000cwz.googlegroups.com...
> Hello,
>
> When Im installing Tru64 on my system I have a 70gb SCSI drive as the
> primary disk and the original 9.1gb scsi drive as the secondary disk. I
> am looking to move a 70gb drive that we have spare into the server. the
> question is can i add that 70gb then use LSM to mirror it or does it
> have to be done from when the  system is installed?
>
> Thanks
>
You can add a drive later on, with AdvFS tools that is. My own system
started off with just two drives, a 2 GB system disk and a 2 GB disk for
data. Next a 4 GB drive was
added and after that a 9 GB disk. It is possible to put them in one large
filesystem domain so as seen from a user point of view the 2 GB data disk
kind of grew to a 15 GB volume.
The tool (Motif based) is rather intuitive. I'm more familiar with VMS but
it took me an hour or so to figure this out.

Hans




